                <h2>Pre-Setup: Define Your Fund Management Metrics</h2>
<p>Before executing this SOP, your team must align on the following core metrics:</p>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Metric</th>
<th>Formula</th>
<th>Healthy Threshold</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>Daily Spend Rate</td>
<td>Daily Spend ÷ Account Balance</td>
<td>Varies by budget size</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Top-up Timeliness</td>
<td>Actual Top-up Time ÷ Planned Top-up Time</td>
<td>≥95%</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Balance Alert Rate</td>
<td>Alert Triggers ÷ Operating Days</td>
<td>≤15%</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Reconciliation Variance</td>
<td>Variance Amount ÷ Total Spend</td>
<td>≤0.5%</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<p>Import these metrics into your internal dashboard and review key data during daily stand-ups.</p>
<hr />
<h2>Step 1 Account Configuration &amp; Budget Allocation</h2>
<p><strong>1.1 Establish Independent Account Structures by Platform</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>Set up separate accounts for Meta Ads Manager, TikTok Ads, Google Ads, etc.</li>
<li>Define a daily budget cap for each account at 1.2-1.5x the expected daily spend</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>1.2 Configure Top-up Channels &amp; Payment Methods</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>Corporate accounts should prioritize bank transfers or corporate credit cards</li>
<li>Third-party escrow accounts (e.g., Yiyu platform) enable unified balance visibility across multiple accounts</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>1.3 Implement Permission Hierarchy</strong></p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Admin</strong>: Full top-up and budget modification rights</li>
<li><strong>Operations</strong>: Read-only access to spend data, no top-up rights</li>
<li><strong>Finance</strong>: Read-only access to reconciliation reports, no ad operation rights</li>
</ul>
<blockquote>
<p>Permission separation is fundamental to fund risk control and prevents errors caused by single-person operations.</p>
</blockquote>
<hr />
<h2>Step 2 Daily Fund Monitoring</h2>
<p><strong>2.1 Daily Checklist</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>[ ] Platform account balances and today's spend</li>
<li>[ ] Whether spend velocity is within normal range</li>
<li>[ ] Any abnormal large spend transactions</li>
<li>[ ] Planned top-ups for today</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>2.2 Abnormal Spend Velocity Detection</strong></p>
<p>When hourly spend exceeds 1.5x the daily average, investigate immediately:</p>
<ol>
<li>Any high-budget campaigns accidentally activated?</li>
<li>Possible malicious clicking?</li>
<li>Campaign/creative breakout?</li>
</ol>
<p><strong>2.3 Balance Health Assessment</strong></p>
<p>Assess "Days of Spend Remaining" daily:</p>
<pre><code>Days Remaining = Current Balance ÷ 7-Day Average Daily Spend
</code></pre>
<ul>
<li>Days Remaining ≤ 2: Immediate top-up required</li>
<li>Days Remaining 3-5: Top-up within today</li>
<li>Days Remaining &gt; 5: Normal operations</li>
</ul>
<hr />
<h2>Step 3 Top-up Management &amp; Balance Alerts</h2>
<p><strong>3.1 Top-up Approval Workflow</strong></p>
<ol>
<li>Operations submits top-up request (platform, account, amount, reason)</li>
<li>Finance verifies budget alignment with monthly spend plan</li>
<li>Admin executes top-up</li>
<li>Record top-up voucher and confirmation time</li>
</ol>
<p><strong>3.2 Balance Alert Configuration</strong></p>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Alert Level</th>
<th>Trigger Condition</th>
<th>Response Time</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>Red Alert</td>
<td>Balance &lt; 3 days expected spend</td>
<td>Within 2 hours</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Orange Alert</td>
<td>Balance &lt; 5 days expected spend</td>
<td>Within same day</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Yellow Alert</td>
<td>Balance &lt; 7 days expected spend</td>
<td>Within 48 hours</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<p><strong>3.3 Top-up Channel Selection</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>Bank Transfer: Suitable for large amounts, 1-3 business days processing</li>
<li>Online Payment: Suitable for urgent small amounts, transaction fees apply</li>
<li>Third-party Escrow: Supports shared balance across multiple accounts, ideal for multi-account teams</li>
</ul>
<hr />
<h2>Step 4 Financial Reconciliation Process</h2>
<p><strong>4.1 Weekly Reconciliation Checklist</strong></p>
<ol>
<li><strong>Download platform invoices</strong>: Export weekly spend reports from each ad platform</li>
<li><strong>Verify account transactions</strong>: Compare top-up records against platform confirmations</li>
<li><strong>Validate spend data</strong>: Check consistency between platform reports and internal records</li>
<li><strong>Document anomalies</strong>: Investigate and log any discrepancies found</li>
</ol>
<p><strong>4.2 Monthly Reconciliation Standard Actions</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>Complete monthly spend summary and compare against budget</li>
<li>Analyze platform spend distribution changes</li>
<li>Evaluate top-up timeliness and balance alert frequency</li>
<li>Generate monthly fund utilization efficiency report</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>4.3 Handling Reconciliation Variance</strong></p>
<p>If discrepancies are found, investigate in this order:</p>
<ol>
<li>Check for top-up processing delays</li>
<li>Verify any unspent balance returns</li>
<li>Contact platform support to confirm billing</li>
<li>Preserve communication records and update internal ledgers</li>
</ol>
<hr />
<h2>Step 5 Risk Control &amp; Optimization</h2>
<p><strong>5.1 Risk Identification Checklist</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>[ ] Single account daily spend exceeds budget cap by 200%</li>
<li>[ ] Large spend occurring outside business hours</li>
<li>[ ] Multiple top-ups from the same IP in a short period</li>
<li>[ ] Account balance suddenly drops to zero with no activity</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>5.2 Optimization Recommendations</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>Adopt "small frequent top-up" strategy to reduce single-transaction risk</li>
<li>Establish monthly alignment between top-up budgets and spend plans</li>
<li>Prioritize escrow platforms that offer real-time balance monitoring</li>
</ul>
<hr />
<h2>Appendix: Quick FAQ</h2>
<p><strong>Q: What if balance doesn't update after top-up?</strong><br />
Some platforms have processing delays. Keep your voucher and contact platform support if balance hasn't updated within 30 minutes.</p>
<p><strong>Q: Why aren't ads running despite sufficient balance?</strong><br />
Check for platform review holds, whether the balance is pre-authorized funds, and whether your ad credentials remain valid.</p>
<p><strong>Q: How do I know if I need to increase my top-up budget?</strong><br />
When days of spend remaining stays below 5 and you have confirmed scaling plans, increase your top-up budget and notify finance in advance.</p>
